{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2025-7519",
    "CVE-2026-4897"
  ],
  "description": "It was discovered that polkit incorrectly handled nested elements in XML\npolicy files. If an administrator were tricked into installing a malicious\npolicy file, a remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\npolkit to crash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2025-7519)\n\nPavel Kohout discovered that the polkit polkit-agent-helper-1 utility\nincorrectly handled long input. A local attacker could possibly use this\nissue to cause polkit to crash, resulting in a denial of service.\n(CVE-2026-4897)",
  "id": "USN-8173-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in polkit.",
